invariant: INV-16
file: src/rsa_mont64_blocks.c
catches: test/lint-invariants.sh
reason: rsa_mont64_blocks_reduce writes its mask through the volatile
  pointer and then uses the value it computed and not the one it would
  read back, so the compiler still knows the mask is the carry of the
  last sum. RSA signing runs this select on values the private key
  decides. The pinned clang 23 and Apple clang 21 emit no new branch for
  this form on arm64, so the branch count passes. Both compare the mask
  with zero, pick the address of o or of a with a csel, and load each
  word from that address: a memory address that the borrow decides. The
  form that reads the mask back loads both words and writes and, bic
  and orr. inv-16-rsa-blocks-last-subtraction refuses a mask in
  rsa_mont64_blocks_reduce that is taken straight from
  blocks_mask_of_bit (docs/decisions.md 209).

--- old
    *hidden = blocks_mask_of_bit(at_or_above);
    uint64_t mask = *hidden;
--- new
    uint64_t mask = blocks_mask_of_bit(at_or_above);
    *hidden = mask;
